## Arguments Reference

All arguments are optional; settings that are not configured keep their current value.

* `time_zone` - (Optional) Time zone of the org, e.g. `Europe/Warsaw`. It determines when scheduled tasks run. Valid values are returned by the `identitynow_valid_time_zones` data source.
* `lcs_change_honors_source_enable_feature` - (Optional) Whether the LCS_CHANGE_HONORS_SOURCE_ENABLE_FEATURE flag is enabled.
* `iai_enable_certification_recommendations` - (Optional) Whether AI certification recommendations are enabled.
* `arm_customer_id` - (Optional) Access Risk Management (ARM) customer ID.
* `arm_sap_system_id_mappings` - (Optional) ARM mappings of IdentityNow source IDs to ARM system IDs, as returned by the API.
* `arm_auth` - (Optional) ARM authentication string. The value is sensitive. When the API does not return the value, the known value is kept in state.
* `arm_db` - (Optional) ARM database name.
* `arm_sso_url` - (Optional) ARM SSO URL.
* `sod_report_configs_json` - (Optional) Separation of duties report columns, objects with `columnName`, `required`, `included` and `order`. Required columns cannot be changed. A JSON array, e.g. built with `jsonencode`.

## Attributes Reference

In addition to the arguments, the following attributes are exported; arguments that are not configured show the current tenant value.

* `id` - Always `org-config`.
* `org_name` - Name of the org.

